<Ctrl-Z> denotes the single 1AH end-of-console-input character; it is not
part of ADBYTE.PLM. The extracted source round-trips byte-for-byte.

During post-build paper-tape capture, two command-entry attempts lost their
leading characters and ISIS rejected them as `AT, NO SUCH FILE` and
`OPY, NO SUCH FILE`. The intended SAT, OBJ and MAP transfers were retried
successfully. These collection-only errors occurred after compilation and
did not alter the preserved guest artifacts.
